{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/25123-a-couple-of-questions-about-what-is-happening-to-white-wolf","id":25123,"title":"A couple of questions about what is happening to White Wolf","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-07T08:27:11-08:00","id":25123,"title":"A couple of questions about what is happening to White Wolf","content":"1. I haven't played an RPG in a long time, and it's been even longer since I played a WW RPG. The last time was shortly after the new Vampire game was released. So it goes without saying that I'm a little out of touch. Is this Onyx Path Publishing a reinvented White Wolf, or did they buy WW out, or something else? I'm a little confused about what's going on.<br /> <br /> 2. I did formerly drop in once or twice a year to see what was going on in the WW forums, mostly out of nostalgia. May I assume that this is the new &quot;official&quot; forum for the old WW games? And if so, will the other &quot;OWoD&quot; settings (Wraith, Hunter, etc.) get their own forums?<br /> <br /> 3. Is there somewhere that answers these questions in detail? A link would be much appreciated.<br /> <br /> Sorry if all this is common knowledge, I'm very much out of the loop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1567-clockwork-chaos","name":"Clockwork Chaos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T08:51:26-08:00","id":25138,"title":"","content":"1. White Wolf Publishing merged a few years after the launch of the New World of Darkness and Vampire: the Requiem with CCP Games, who obtained the World of Darkness property with the aim of adapting it to a MMORPG; at that point, White Wolf became a label and a subdivision of CCP, and continued to produce games for several years. Around a year ago or so, CCP suffered losses and responded with a heavy wave of layoffs, which gutted the White Wolf subdivision. Rich Thomas, previously the creative director of the White Wolf label, decided to incorporate as Onyx Path Publishing, hiring on a freelance basis those writers whom he had already been hiring as White Wolf director, and obtained the license to produce roleplaying books for both World of Darkness settings and the Exalted setting, as well as full ownership of the Scion and Trinity Universe products. That's where we stand now: &quot;White Wolf&quot; is a name for a subdivision of the owners of the World of Darkness properties, who remain CCP Games and are basically out of the roleplaying supplement business, which has been picked up by Onyx Path Publishing, which is basically another way to refer to Rich Thomas hiring the same people he was already hiring for the same jobs prior to the CCP layoffs.<br /> <br /> Correct me if I'm wrong about any of these details, of course. It's easy to get bits off even if you were paying attention through the whole thing.<br /> <br /> 2. The White Wolf forums have closed down now, and the Onyx Path forums are basically replacing them as the &quot;official&quot; venue for the roleplaying games as such, yeah. Each of the Old World of Darkness gamelines have been receiving a subforum of their own in advance of the production of a 20th Anniversary Edition, so if things follow the pattern set so far, I'd expect a Wraith subforum to be next forthcoming.<br /> <br /> 3. There was a Gencon panel about &quot;what's up with White Wolf/Onyx Path,&quot; I'm not sure whether that's up archived somewhere or not, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T01:33:02-08:00","id":25672,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman\"><b>Stupid Loserman</b></a> has everything about right, as far as I know.<br /> <br /> Every year, and at many conventions that Onyx Path Publishing attends, they have a panel called &quot;What's Up with White Wolf&quot;. This actually goes back quite a few years, actually. The official announcement of what exactly Onyx Path was came at Gen Con 2012 under &quot;What Is the Onyx Path?&quot;. Their first book was actually released months earlier with their logo but it wasn't finalized and revealed until that panel.<br /> <br /> Most of the generally important information about upcoming White Wolf and Onyx Path Publishing books and business can be found on Rich's &quot;<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/news/monday-meeting/\" target=\"_blank\">Monday Meeting Blog</a>&quot; on <a href=\"http://www.TheOnyxPath.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.TheOnyxPath.com</a>. It is typically a run-down of he and Eddy Webb's meetings (Eddy is sort of the liaison between Rich and CCP) and their long friendship and non-business conversations are also included as, well, they are also part of the &quot;meeting&quot;.<br /> <br /> While this is the place where most information is dumped and found at, there are other locations where information is also posted:<br /> <img src=\"http://i1.ytimg.com/u/zN5jRB35OvnC-6gxnRY4gQ/channels4_banner.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/user/TheOnyxPath\" target=\"_blank\"><b>YouTube</b>: TheOnyxPath</a>: Where they post videos from panels, Q&amp;A, KickStarter videos, and more.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/theonyxpath\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Facebook</b>: TheOnyxPath</a><br /> <a href=\"http://reddit.com/r/WhiteWolfRPG\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Reddit</b>: WhiteWolfRPG </a><br /> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/theonyxpath\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Twitter</b>: @TheOnyxPath</a><br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Tumblr</b>: theonyxpath</a><br /> <a href=\"http://gplus.to/TheOnyxPath\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Google+</b>: TheOnyxPath</a><br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/profile/200664283/created\" target=\"_blank\"><b>KickStarter</b>: Richard Thomas</a> (since he's the one who's created each KS so far.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Also</i>, ...<br /> <b>LARP (Mind's Eye Theater)</b>: Richard and Onyx Path Publishing only picked up the licenses for the tabletop RPG stuff (mostly.) The <u>Mind's Eye Theater</u> license was picked up by Shane DeFreest and his company &quot;<a href=\"http://www.bynightstudios.com/\" target=\"_blank\">By Night Stuidos</a>&quot;. They work independently from Onyx Path Publishing (but that doesn't mean that they don't talk amongst themselves either.) They are creating a new system for MET that is very different from the previous versions, but many of their playtest documents and the likes are available and have been given pretty good marks so far. The final rule book is going to be a goddamned TOME though, but I think the intent is to include ALL of the rules in one book, rather than the 40 that each line currently has.<br /> <br /> <b>Ancillary Products</b>: Both OPP and BNS must have their projects approved by CCP, from concept to final product. CCP has also been very restrictive (or, at least has not easily thrown around the licensed approval) to produce other products that contain the trademarked logos and such from White Wolf. There have been exceptions (like By Night Studios producing a limited run of Clan pins for their &quot;Mind's Eye Theater: Vampire the Masquerade&quot; KickStarter), but no one, that I know of, has the rights to produce shirts, mugs, rings, etc. with the glyphs/logos/etc. from the games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T13:59:53-08:00","id":26020,"title":"","content":"1. Stupid Loserman has it right. CCP hit a rough patch, and laid off a lot of us. It was a pretty dark day, but within hours of being laid off I was on the phone with Rich talking about the new schedule. The guy moves fast.<br /> <br /> Rich started Onyx and brought several of us back in as freelancers. Eddy Webb stayed at CCP and became our liaison. We launched the most ambitious White Wolf schedule in years, with an overhaul for Vampire: The Requiem, new World of Darkness lines in the form of Mummy and Demon, and new editions for Apocalypse, Oblivion, and Exalted. There have been some delays, but we're producing a lot more books now than we were towards the end of our stay at CCP. CCP gives us a pretty free hand, creatively, so we've kept on doing what we're good at.<br /> <br /> We produce the World of Darkness and Exalted under license from CCP. Rich bought Scion, Trinity, and Scarred Lands outright. Onyx will also be publishing other lines, such as my game Cavaliers of Mars.<br /> <br /> 2. Yes, this is the official forum for White Wolf roleplaying games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Torakhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/25123-a-couple-of-questions-about-what-is-happening-to-white-wolf?p=25672#post25672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ancillary Products</b>: Both OPP and BNS must have their projects approved by CCP, from concept to final product. CCP has also been very restrictive (or, at least has not easily thrown around the licensed approval) to produce other products that contain the trademarked logos and such from White Wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>CCP has been pretty permissive, actually, and our license allows us to do more than we have the bandwidth for.<br /> <br /> We can't do merchandise right now for logistical reasons, though. Everything we do is made to order, either as part of a limited edition or as an on-demand product. Doing stuff like t-shirts would require us to maintain an inventory, which we're not set up for. As sentimental as I am about the old White Wolf warehouse, maintaining it was a bear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 12-08-2013, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T16:40:32-08:00","id":26121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/25123-a-couple-of-questions-about-what-is-happening-to-white-wolf?p=26020#post26020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or as an on-demand product. Doing stuff like t-shirts would require us to maintain an inventory, which we're not set up for.</div> </div> </div> </div>T-shirts can be done via On-Demand as well. In fact, putting &quot;On-Demand Shirts&quot; on Google gave me instant hits like Shirtbot or Teesondemand, mass etc.<br /> But I expect you guys would want any sort of &quot;On-Demand Shirts&quot; service to be part of DrivethruRPG.com: Like Drivethrufiction and Drivethrucards are.<br /> Definitely something to pitch towards the DrivethruRPG.com guys, though.<br /> <br /> Also there would be a question of what to use for printing &quot;On-Demand Shirts&quot;. I have a feeling transfer sheets would used over silkscreening. Nothing wrong with transfer sheets, but as someone who has worked with the medium: I love silk screened shirts more.<br /> <br /> But this makes me wonder whatever happened to Java Crypt. Back in the day, Java would do jewelry products for White Wolf's game logos (Clans and Tribes). And way before that, Chessex used to make products for White Wolf like Book covers and glasses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T19:03:58-08:00","id":26207,"title":"","content":"What I'd meant is that (from what I had heard earlier) the licenses didn't cover &quot;other&quot; materials using the White Wolf IP that weren't necessarily &quot;tabletop RP&quot; related... so while dice-roller programs and stuff would be covered under that, even getting pins and the likes for the KS, or whatnot (as BNS did) required special permission from CCP.<br /> <br /> There are actually Print-on-Demand Tshirt companies that use a sort of inkjet printer that use silkscreen paint and print right onto the Tshirts (and their quality looked damn good, though I don't know how they hold-up to washes and wear.)<br /> Printing on white shirts is easy, but printing on a black shirt requires a layer of white to be laid down under the color, and one company that my print shop was looking into had only made one, and it was for their own promotional work--no one had actually bought one that printed on black yet. That was about 5 years ago though, so I don't know if that's still the case. I agree that transfers suck, though I actually think that VistaPrint can print directly to shirts too, but if you have to &quot;cut out&quot; the black background, or add a border, unless you want to see a black box around something.<br /> <br /> I've talked with Rich about doing posters, but he isn't (wasn't) happy with the quality of print-on-demand posters yet (that was while talking to him at Gen Con 2012, so things may have changed.) IF Rich can find a PoD print company that can do high enough quality prints, I really think that uploading the artwork files and letting them do all of the work would let him upload all sorts of cool artwork (even old book covers and stuff) that folks can purchase if they want, and all he'd have to do is send the files. Apparently DriveThruRPG is talking to someone about doing ST screens PoD too, but I think that's still in the early talks.<br /> <br /> I'd love to see more companies grabbing licenses to provide stuff using the trademarks and identities in the White Wolf IP. Laser-engraved items and such would be awesome to have available...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T23:32:04-08:00","id":26330,"title":"","content":"I know things like shirts aren't a priority or even in the pipeline right now, but:<br /> <br /> It'd be cool to women's/babydoll shirts of any design that's offered, in the theoretical future where this happens. Lots of ladies game, and most us stopped wearing men's/boys' shirts (no, they NOT unisex) sometime around puberty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Demon Cat</b></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://flamingporcupine.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Illuminated Dark Ages character sheets and more</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10-demon-cat","name":"Demon Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"266"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T01:20:28-08:00","id":27829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/25123-a-couple-of-questions-about-what-is-happening-to-white-wolf?p=26330#post26330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know things like shirts aren't a priority or even in the pipeline right now, but:<br /> <br /> It'd be cool to women's/babydoll shirts of any design that's offered, in the theoretical future where this happens. Lots of ladies game, and most us stopped wearing men's/boys' shirts (no, they NOT unisex) sometime around puberty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Some of my most treasured shirts are my <i>Requiem</i> baby doll tees.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T10:18:00-08:00","id":28075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/25123-a-couple-of-questions-about-what-is-happening-to-white-wolf?p=26020#post26020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Stupid Loserman has it right. CCP hit a rough patch, and laid off a lot of us. It was a pretty dark day, but within hours of being laid off I was on the phone with Rich talking about the new schedule. The guy moves fast.<br /> <br /> Rich started Onyx and brought several of us back in as freelancers. Eddy Webb stayed at CCP and became our liaison. We launched the most ambitious White Wolf schedule in years, with an overhaul for Vampire: The Requiem, new World of Darkness lines in the form of Mummy and Demon, and new editions for Apocalypse, Oblivion, and Exalted. There have been some delays, but we're producing a lot more books now than we were towards the end of our stay at CCP. CCP gives us a pretty free hand, creatively, so we've kept on doing what we're good at.<br /> <br /> We produce the World of Darkness and Exalted under license from CCP. Rich bought Scion, Trinity, and Scarred Lands outright. Onyx will also be publishing other lines, such as my game Cavaliers of Mars.<br /> <br /> 2. Yes, this is the official forum for White Wolf roleplaying games.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> CCP has been pretty permissive, actually, and our license allows us to do more than we have the bandwidth for.<br /> <br /> We can't do merchandise right now for logistical reasons, though. Everything we do is made to order, either as part of a limited edition or as an on-demand product. Doing stuff like t-shirts would require us to maintain an inventory, which we're not set up for. As sentimental as I am about the old White Wolf warehouse, maintaining it was a bear.</div> </div> </div> </div>New Apocalypse and Oblivion Editions! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> do just mean the 20th ed stuff or.... &gt;<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T11:09:11-08:00","id":28114,"title":"","content":"Eldagusto, considering Werewolf 20th is just now shipping, Mage 20th is just finishing up being written, Wraith 20th is maybe at the outline stage, and Changeling 20th is neither confirmed nor denied, I'd be willing to bet Rose meant the 20th Anniversary Editions <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T14:20:04-08:00","id":28924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/25123-a-couple-of-questions-about-what-is-happening-to-white-wolf?p=28075#post28075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> New Apocalypse and Oblivion Editions! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> do just mean the 20th ed stuff or.... &gt;<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> I meant the anniversary editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T01:38:32-08:00","id":29202,"title":"","content":"Thanks to all for the info and links. I don't have the time these days to indulge, but I've got a lot of great memories from yesteryear. I'm glad to know that White Wolf is continuing in spirit, if not name.<br /> <br /> Another couple quick questions: is Onyx Path redoing everything White Wolf put out, or just updating the core rules? Are they putting out new stuff? If they're putting out new stuff, where in the timeline would it fall? And did CCP (or Onyx Path) also get the rights to the Black Dog stuff too, which to my limited understanding was somehow a separate company?<br /> <br /> With regards to tshirts, I can tell you that modern print-on-demand technology gives you very high quality and durable tshirts. These days you can even select from a range of brands and styles for each individual tshirt. A group of my friends print group tshirts for birthdays and other events, as well as individual ones for gifts and jokes. We've been doing it since late 2009 or so, and the oldest ones are still perfectly wearable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1567,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1567-clockwork-chaos","user":"Clockwork Chaos","date":". 12-13-2013, 04:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1567-clockwork-chaos","name":"Clockwork Chaos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T03:00:26-08:00","id":29219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clockwork Chaos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/25123-a-couple-of-questions-about-what-is-happening-to-white-wolf?p=29202#post29202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another couple quick questions: is Onyx Path redoing everything White Wolf put out, or just updating the core rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not everything (since I'm sure that a new Street Fighter RPG isn't a reasonable expectation).<br /> <br /> And I don't think Onyx Path knows exactly how much of the old material they're going to &quot;redo&quot; or even what counts as &quot;redoing&quot; it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are they putting out new stuff? </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If they're putting out new stuff, where in the timeline would it fall? And did CCP (or Onyx Path) also get the rights to the Black Dog stuff too, which to my limited understanding was somehow a separate company? </div> </div> </div>There's a tentative schedule on the main webpage addressing what books are in the pipeline.<br /> <br /> CCP got the rights to Black Dog because Black Dog was never a separate company. It was an alternate imprint owned by WW. Onyx Path could, technically, make Black Dog material if they felt like it, and got it approved by CCP, but it seems unlikely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T06:06:23-08:00","id":29266,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the quick reply. One clarification though: when I asked about the timeline, I meant the metaplot of the old WoD. I.e. is it before the Week of Nightmares? After Gehenna?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1567-clockwork-chaos","name":"Clockwork Chaos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T06:26:22-08:00","id":29275,"title":"","content":"I believe the position of the 20th Anniversary books is to take an ambiguous stance on that \u2014 that is, provide material that works whether you're setting games before the Week of Nightmares, after the Week of Nightmares, after when the Gehenna book was set, etc. There's no post-Gehenna material, which is to say, there's material that works set up to the modern day, but it assumes that the events of Gehenna failed to transpire at that time, and may or may not still be forthcoming.<br /> <br /> That last answer is, I think, what the new material, such as the Revised Convention Books for Mage, went with \u2014 the Red Star came, the Avatar Storm struck, everything was building to a crescendo and then... the world just continued as it was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T12:06:57-08:00","id":29449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/25123-a-couple-of-questions-about-what-is-happening-to-white-wolf?p=29219#post29219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">CCP got the rights to Black Dog because Black Dog was never a separate company. It was an alternate imprint owned by WW. Onyx Path could, technically, make Black Dog material if they felt like it, and got it approved by CCP, but it seems unlikely.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Demon: The Descent Kickstarter, there was a comment explaining why they won't use Black Dog anymore.<br /> Basically, Black Dog was used back in the day after the issue with Clanbook: Tzimisce's backcover. And the books were not bought by some Game Stores because of the imprint, while others that did buy the imprint had to hide them away so younger customers wouldn't just grab them. Remember, this was back in the day when people protested or boycotted companies and stores because, &quot;Satan&quot;, &quot;RPGs are evil and teach you magic&quot; nonsense.<br /> I even have a White Wolf magazine issue that reported a store having trouble because the religious person complaining/protesting was upset over them selling W:tA.<br /> POD does away with that, so there's no need for the imprint anymore.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T12:48:19-08:00","id":29468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clockwork Chaos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/25123-a-couple-of-questions-about-what-is-happening-to-white-wolf?p=29202#post29202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks to all for the info and links. I don't have the time these days to indulge, but I've got a lot of great memories from yesteryear. I'm glad to know that White Wolf is continuing in spirit, if not name.</div> </div> </div> </div>All World of Darkness and Exalted products will continue to have the White Wolf logo. They'll just also include an Onyx Path logo. Former WW stuff like Scion and the Trinity Continuum will just have an Onyx Path logo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another couple quick questions: is Onyx Path redoing everything White Wolf put out, or just updating the core rules? Are they putting out new stuff? If they're putting out new stuff, where in the timeline would it fall? And did CCP (or Onyx Path) also get the rights to the Black Dog stuff too, which to my limited understanding was somehow a separate company? </div> </div> </div>Assuming you're talking about just the Classic World of Darkness when you say &quot;everything WW put out,&quot; we're examining whether 20th anniversary releases make sense on a year-by-year basis. Existing material is available in PDF and print-on-demand via DriveThruRPG; we have no reason to reprint existing material if it's all available already. We've released a handful of additional books for Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage, with more to come. See our Schedule page for details.<br /> <br /> The new books are metaplot-agnostic. They're at an undefined point somewhere around the cusp of 2e and Revised.<br /> <br /> Black Dog was an imprint of White Wolf, not a separate company. We could do new Black Dog material if we wanted, but there's really no reason to with the current market.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With regards to tshirts, I can tell you that modern print-on-demand technology gives you very high quality and durable tshirts. These days you can even select from a range of brands and styles for each individual tshirt. A group of my friends print group tshirts for birthdays and other events, as well as individual ones for gifts and jokes. We've been doing it since late 2009 or so, and the oldest ones are still perfectly wearable. </div> </div> </div>Managing this at the moment would require additional resources, while we're trying to catch up our late books with our already full schedule. Maybe someday, but not now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":4,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","user":"IanWatson","date":". 12-13-2013, 11:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T00:55:08-08:00","id":29798,"title":"","content":"Some things to add to Ian's post though:<br /> <br /> Yeah, <b>Black Dog Game Factory</b> was a name for their &quot;adult&quot; works. With PoD, it's not really necessary, though it would be kind of nice to keep as a way of &quot;rating&quot; a book as &quot;intensely inappropriate for normal people.&quot; However, they WILL make an appearance in &quot;Book of the Wyrm: 20th Anniversary Edition&quot;, though they will have been bought out by an even more evil Icelandic company... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>As for the &quot;continuity&quot; of the books being released?</b> There are a FEW CWoD books that have been released lately (or the near future) that still exist within the Revised, or Dark Ages rules/continuity and aren't part of the 20th Anniversary gamelines...<br /> <br /> Recently, the Revised Convention Books were released for &quot;Mage: the Ascension Revised Edition.&quot; These books (available on DriveThruRPG) include <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/107693/Convention-Book-NWO\" target=\"_blank\">New World Order</a>, <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/113471/Convention-Book-Progenitors\" target=\"_blank\">Progenitors</a>, <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/117395/Convention-Book-Syndicate\" target=\"_blank\">Syndicate</a>, and <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/120616/Convention-Book-Void-Engineers\" target=\"_blank\">Void Engineers</a> (Revised <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/3041/Convention-Book-Iteration-X?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Iteration X</a> was released in January 2002). These books actually take place &quot;Today&quot;, a decade after the &quot;Time of Judgement&quot;, and (so far) are the only official continuation of the &quot;story&quot; of the Classic World of Darkness (at least from the sphere of Mage: the Ascension) that we've gotten. The N.W.O. book is pretty enlightening, as it talks about the Vampires supposedly waiting for their legends to return and... nothing happened. Meanwhile, Humanity has not only accepted what the N.W.O. has told them, but basically taken the ball and ran with it and now they're trying to figure out WTF is going on and are split up on whether this is how things should be (humanity closing in on ascension as they create &quot;magic&quot; through beliving just about anything), or if they need to somehow control the masses (it's hard to give up that power, you know?) ... we've gone from 60-minute tape-players on our hips to devices the size of watches that can carry thousands of hours of audio, beamed directly to ear pieces and communicate with our pocket-computers we call &quot;cell phones.&quot; ...<br /> <br /> For Dark Ages Vampire: we have &quot;Dark Ages: Darkening Sky&quot; which was a book that was promised, but never published back in the day. 160 pages, or so, with 5 chapters, each covering one of the fatsplats (Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, Inquisitors, Fae) regarding the eclipse of 1230AD. This isn't for V20: Dark Ages, but for the original Dark Ages line.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, everything else CWoD is geared towards the 20th Anniversary Editions, which are all set in an ambiguous &quot;today&quot;, without a strong metaplot, and sort of sets a lot of the &quot;story themes&quot; back just before the Time of Judgement and more towards the 2nd Edition era (Sam Haight is dead, but Albrecht is still Lord, not King, Stargazers are still part of the Nation, and Black Tooth is still alive, but the Ahadi are around... so there's a bit of of a jog back and to the left.) However, it really tries to leave as many options open to the ST as possible by including not only info, but mechanics for lost Tribes as well as lost Fera too. (If you pick up a Print-on-Demand copy, I HIGHLY suggest the Premium Color... it's costly, but it's about as close to traditional printing as you'll get, aside from the KickStarter Deluxe Editions that ACTUALLY use traditional printing.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","user":"Torakhan","date":". 12-14-2013, 04:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T13:51:21-08:00","id":30090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/25123-a-couple-of-questions-about-what-is-happening-to-white-wolf?p=29219#post29219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> CCP got the rights to Black Dog because Black Dog was never a separate company. It was an alternate imprint owned by WW. Onyx Path could, technically, make Black Dog material if they felt like it, and got it approved by CCP, but it seems unlikely.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understand it, the Black Dog imprint is pretty irrelevant these days, as it was intended as a &quot;Mature Readers&quot; label at a time when White Wolf had to be concerned with dealing with community standards at the local bookstore and RPGs were still not too far removed from the Satanic Panic of the 80s and 90s. Since Onyx Path is primarily direct to consumer and the standards of what is available at the local Barnes and Nobles has changed a bit, Black Dog is no longer necessary.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/260-chase-variant","name":"Chase Variant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar260_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}